        "Will J. Percival"
      ],
      "assessment": {
        "nobel_worthiness": "BAO converted early-universe sound waves into a robust standard ruler for measuring cosmic expansion and dark energy.",
        "attribution": "Eisenstein, Cole, and Percival were central to the observational extraction and establishment of the method; foundational theoretical credit is broader.",
        "maturity": "The ruler has been repeatedly measured by independent surveys and is now a core cosmological probe.",
        "uncertainties": [
